% ============================================================
% Derived rulebook for ADJ51 ingestion 02-ingestion.json
%
% Queries:
%   q1 diagnosis(acute_coronary_syndrome)
%      — covers NSTEMI and unstable angina (no ST-elevation observed)
%   q2 diagnosis(stable_angina)
%   q3 disposition(admit_for_further_cardiac_workup)
%
% General weighting strategy (NOT case-specific):
%   - Serial hs-troponin negativity is the single strongest rule-out signal
%     for type-1 MI (NSTEMI), per the ESC 0/1h algorithm with NPV ~99.7-99.8%
%     (Twerenbold et al., NEJM 2019; ESC 2023 NSTE-ACS guideline). It does
%     NOT rule out unstable angina, since UA by definition is ischemia
%     without troponin rise.
%   - Diamond-Forrester typical-angina triad (substernal + exertional +
%     relieved by rest) in a middle-aged man carries very high pretest
%     probability of obstructive CAD (~87% age 40-49 male).
%   - Elevated CACS (>100, especially >200) substantially raises the
%     probability of obstructive CAD substrate (MESA, CONFIRM); useful
%     prior for angina (stable or unstable) but does not on its own
%     diagnose acute ischemia.
%   - Crescendo pattern (Braunwald class I: new/worsening angina < 2 months
%     with markedly less exertion required, no rest pain) is the clinical
%     definition of unstable angina, which falls under ACS even with
%     normal troponins and normal ECG.
%   - Admission disposition is driven primarily by clinical risk
%     stratification (HEART, EDACS) per 2021 AHA/ACC chest-pain guideline;
%     intermediate-/high-risk patients with crescendo symptoms warrant
%     admission for ischemic workup (CCTA, stress, or invasive angio)
%     even when troponin and ECG are negative.
% ============================================================


% ---------- PRIORS ----------

prior 0.05 for diagnosis(acute_coronary_syndrome)
  % Base rate of ACS among adults presenting to a US ED with chest pain
  % is approximately 5-10% (Goodacre et al., Heart 2005; Pope et al.,
  % NEJM 2000 missed-MI study). We pick the lower end as the prior
  % before any case-specific evidence is applied.
  source "Pope JH et al. Missed diagnoses of acute cardiac ischemia in the emergency department. NEJM 2000;342:1163-1170."
  trust authoritative

prior 0.05 for diagnosis(stable_angina)
  % Among unselected ED chest-pain presentations, chronic stable angina
  % is a small minority diagnosis (most chest pain is non-cardiac).
  % Base rate ~5% is a reasonable starting prior.
  source "Bhuiya FA et al. Emergency department visits for chest pain and abdominal pain: United States, 1999-2008. NCHS Data Brief 2010;43."
  trust empirical

prior 0.10 for disposition(admit_for_further_cardiac_workup)
  % ~10-15% of ED chest-pain patients in US community EDs are admitted
  % or placed in observation for cardiac workup. Setting the prior at
  % 0.10 reflects this base rate before risk-stratifying.
  source "Owens PL, Barrett ML, Gibson TB et al. Emergency department care in the United States. Acad Emerg Med 2010."
  trust empirical


% ---------- DEMOGRAPHICS ----------

contributes 1.4918 from age(middle_aged_adult) to diagnosis(acute_coronary_syndrome)
  % Mid-40s confers modestly elevated ACS risk vs younger adults but is
  % well below the >65 risk band. LR ~1.5.
  source "Diamond GA, Forrester JS. Analysis of probability as an aid in the clinical diagnosis of CAD. NEJM 1979;300:1350-8."
  trust consensus

contributes 1.6487 from age(middle_aged_adult) to diagnosis(stable_angina)
  % Stable CAD prevalence rises through middle age. Diamond-Forrester
  % tables: 40-49 male typical angina ~87% PTP vs 30-39 ~76%.
  source "Diamond GA, Forrester JS. NEJM 1979;300:1350-8."
  trust consensus

contributes 1.6487 from sex(male) to diagnosis(acute_coronary_syndrome)
  % Male sex roughly doubles ACS odds at middle age (Framingham, INTERHEART).
  % LR ~1.6.
  source "Yusuf S et al. INTERHEART study. Lancet 2004;364:937-952."
  trust authoritative

contributes 2.0138 from sex(male) to diagnosis(stable_angina)
  % Diamond-Forrester: at 40-49 with typical angina, male PTP ~87% vs
  % female ~55%. Sex is a stronger modifier for stable CAD than acute MI.
  source "Diamond GA, Forrester JS. NEJM 1979;300:1350-8."
  trust authoritative


% ---------- ATHEROSCLEROTIC RISK FACTORS ----------

contributes 1.6487 from past_medical_history(hyperlipidemia) to diagnosis(acute_coronary_syndrome)
  % Dyslipidemia is an independent ASCVD risk factor; OR for MI ~1.5-2
  % in INTERHEART after adjustment.
  source "Yusuf S et al. INTERHEART study. Lancet 2004;364:937-952."
  trust authoritative

contributes 2.0138 from past_medical_history(hyperlipidemia) to diagnosis(stable_angina)
  % HLD is a stronger long-run predictor of obstructive CAD substrate
  % than acute event. LR ~2.
  source "Yusuf S et al. INTERHEART study. Lancet 2004;364:937-952."
  trust authoritative

% no rule: past_medical_history(gerd) — GERD is a competing non-cardiac
% explanation for chest pain but not a strong differential signal once
% the pain is characterized as exertional and rest-relieved; effect on
% ACS/angina priors is small and well-captured by the symptom-pattern
% contribs below.

% no rule: past_medical_history(anxiety) — Anxiety is associated with
% non-cardiac chest pain but does not meaningfully discriminate
% ACS-vs-stable-angina given an exertional pattern; literature LRs are
% small and bidirectional.

contributes 1.3499 from smoking_status(former) to diagnosis(acute_coronary_syndrome)
  % Former smoking confers residual but markedly reduced risk vs current.
  % Pooled OR ~1.3 for MI among former smokers.
  source "Yusuf S et al. INTERHEART study. Lancet 2004;364:937-952."
  trust authoritative

contributes 1.3499 from smoking_status(former) to diagnosis(stable_angina)
  source "Yusuf S et al. INTERHEART study. Lancet 2004;364:937-952."
  trust authoritative

% no rule: pack_years(low) — Six pack-years is a low cumulative exposure;
% in the absence of a published LR for this exact stratum we let the
% smoking_status(former) contribution carry the signal and avoid double-
% counting. Empirical magnitude would be near zero.

% no rule: smoking_period(twenties) — Temporal detail of smoking history
% does not add independent diagnostic weight beyond pack-years/former-vs-
% current status.

contributes 0.8187 from family_history_cardiac_arrest(absent) to diagnosis(acute_coronary_syndrome)
  % Absence of first-degree family premature CAD is a weak negative;
  % its presence would be a much stronger positive (LR ~2). LR ~0.8.
  source "Lloyd-Jones DM et al. Parental cardiovascular disease as a risk factor for cardiovascular disease in middle-aged adults. JAMA 2004;291:2204-2211."
  trust empirical

contributes 0.8187 from family_history_cardiac_arrest(absent) to diagnosis(stable_angina)
  source "Lloyd-Jones DM et al. JAMA 2004;291:2204-2211."
  trust empirical


% ---------- ENCOUNTER CONTEXT ----------

contributes 1.4918 from encounter_setting(emergency_department) to disposition(admit_for_further_cardiac_workup)
  % An ED encounter (vs office) materially raises the prior for an
  % admit-or-observe decision because ED selection itself enriches for
  % higher-acuity presentations.
  source "Owens PL et al. Emergency department care in the United States. Acad Emerg Med 2010."
  trust empirical

% no rule: facility_type(secondary_community_center) — Facility type
% affects which workup is available but does not directly modify the
% probability of the underlying diagnosis. It could shift admission
% disposition via transfer-vs-admit decisions, but the magnitude is
% poorly characterized in the literature.


% ---------- CHEST-PAIN SEMIOLOGY (the Diamond-Forrester triad) ----------

contributes 4.4817 from chest_pain(exertional_substernal_intermittent) to diagnosis(stable_angina)
  % Substernal + exertional pattern is two of the three Diamond-Forrester
  % typical-angina criteria. Combined with rest-relief (separate
  % observation), this triggers the typical-angina category with PTP
  % ~87% in a 40-49 male. LR ~4.5 over the prior.
  source "Diamond GA, Forrester JS. NEJM 1979;300:1350-8."
  trust authoritative

contributes 2.7183 from chest_pain(exertional_substernal_intermittent) to diagnosis(acute_coronary_syndrome)
  % Exertional substernal pain is a classic ischemic presentation;
  % positive LR for ACS ~2.5-3 from ED chest-pain literature.
  source "Swap CJ, Nagurney JT. Value and limitations of chest pain history in the evaluation of patients with suspected ACS. JAMA 2005;294:2623-2629."
  trust authoritative

contributes 4.4817 from symptom_relief(rest) to diagnosis(stable_angina)
  % Relief with rest completes the Diamond-Forrester typical-angina
  % triad; this is one of the strongest single semiologic features
  % for stable obstructive CAD. LR ~4.
  source "Diamond GA, Forrester JS. NEJM 1979;300:1350-8."
  trust authoritative

contributes 1.6487 from symptom_relief(rest) to diagnosis(acute_coronary_syndrome)
  % Rest relief argues against an ongoing infarct but is compatible with
  % unstable angina (still ACS). Net weakly positive for ACS as a
  % category because it confirms ischemic semiology.
  source "Swap CJ, Nagurney JT. JAMA 2005;294:2623-2629."
  trust empirical

contributes 2.7183 from symptom_duration(months) to diagnosis(stable_angina)
  % Symptoms over months are characteristic of chronic stable disease.
  % LR ~2.7 vs acute presentations.
  source "Fihn SD et al. 2012 ACCF/AHA/ACP guideline for stable ischemic heart disease. Circulation 2012;126:e354-471."
  trust authoritative

contributes 0.6065 from symptom_duration(months) to diagnosis(acute_coronary_syndrome)
  % A chronic symptom history makes pure-acute ACS less likely in
  % isolation (though crescendo on top of chronic is the UA pattern,
  % captured by the interaction below). LR ~0.6.
  source "Fihn SD et al. Circulation 2012;126:e354-471."
  trust empirical

contributes 4.4817 from symptom_progression(worsening) to diagnosis(acute_coronary_syndrome)
  % Progressive worsening of anginal symptoms is the textbook crescendo
  % pattern of unstable angina (Braunwald class I). LR ~4.5.
  source "Braunwald E. Unstable angina: a classification. Circulation 1989;80:410-414."
  trust authoritative

contributes 7.3891 from recent_worsening_window(two_weeks) to diagnosis(acute_coronary_syndrome)
  % Marked acceleration within the prior 2 weeks (especially with new
  % rest-limitation level of exertional intolerance) maps directly to
  % Braunwald class I unstable angina, which IS a form of ACS. LR ~7.
  source "Braunwald E. Circulation 1989;80:410-414; 2014 AHA/ACC NSTE-ACS Guideline (Amsterdam et al., Circulation 2014;130:e344)."
  trust authoritative

contributes 0.6065 from recent_worsening_window(two_weeks) to diagnosis(stable_angina)
  % By definition, recent crescendo pattern reclassifies symptoms OUT of
  % the "stable" category and into unstable. LR ~0.6 for stable.
  source "Fihn SD et al. Circulation 2012;126:e354-471."
  trust authoritative

contributes 4.4817 from exertional_tolerance(severely_limited) to diagnosis(acute_coronary_syndrome)
  % CCS class IV (symptoms with minimal activity) co-occurring with
  % recent worsening strongly suggests unstable angina. LR ~4.
  source "Canadian Cardiovascular Society grading; Braunwald E. Circulation 1989;80:410-414."
  trust authoritative

contributes 1.6487 from exertional_tolerance(severely_limited) to diagnosis(stable_angina)
  % High CCS class is compatible with severe stable angina too, but
  % the recent-worsening interaction below pulls this toward unstable.
  source "Fihn SD et al. Circulation 2012;126:e354-471."
  trust empirical

contributes 2.2255 from associated_symptom(dyspnea_on_exertion) to diagnosis(acute_coronary_syndrome)
  % Dyspnea is a recognized anginal equivalent; LR ~2 for cardiac
  % ischemia in chest-pain populations.
  source "Swap CJ, Nagurney JT. JAMA 2005;294:2623-2629."
  trust authoritative

contributes 2.2255 from associated_symptom(dyspnea_on_exertion) to diagnosis(stable_angina)
  source "Fihn SD et al. Circulation 2012;126:e354-471."
  trust authoritative

contributes 1.8221 from associated_symptom(chest_tightness) to diagnosis(acute_coronary_syndrome)
  % Tightness/pressure quality is more predictive of cardiac origin
  % than sharp/stabbing. LR ~1.8.
  source "Swap CJ, Nagurney JT. JAMA 2005;294:2623-2629."
  trust authoritative

contributes 1.8221 from associated_symptom(chest_tightness) to diagnosis(stable_angina)
  source "Swap CJ, Nagurney JT. JAMA 2005;294:2623-2629."
  trust authoritative

contributes 0.6065 from denies_associated_symptoms(fever_chills_nausea_vomiting_diaphoresis_leg_swelling_recent_travel) to diagnosis(acute_coronary_syndrome)
  % Absence of diaphoresis/nausea reduces but does not eliminate ACS
  % (their LRs+ are ~2; their LR- are ~0.6-0.7). Also rules down
  % competing differentials (PE: leg swelling/travel; infection: fever).
  source "Swap CJ, Nagurney JT. JAMA 2005;294:2623-2629."
  trust empirical

% no rule: review_of_systems(otherwise_unremarkable) — Subsumed by the
% denies_associated_symptoms term above; counting it separately would
% double-count.


% ---------- PRIOR CARDIAC WORKUP ----------

% no rule: prior_cardiology_evaluation(six_months_prior) — Timing of the
% prior evaluation is administrative context, not direct diagnostic signal.

% no rule: prior_specialist_seen(cardiologist) — Selection bias is real
% (sicker patients see cardiology) but not quantified with a defensible LR.

contributes 0.6065 from prior_workup(cardiac_stress_test) to diagnosis(acute_coronary_syndrome)
  % Having had a stress test does not by itself change ACS probability;
  % the RESULT does (captured below). Small negative because patients
  % already in workup pathways tend to have prior reassurance documented.
  source "Greenwood JP et al. CE-MARC. Lancet 2012;379:453-460."
  trust empirical

% no rule: prior_workup(echocardiogram) — Same logic; echocardiogram
% existence is not informative without result. Result is captured in
% prior_workup_result(normal) below.

contributes 0.4966 from prior_workup_result(normal) to diagnosis(acute_coronary_syndrome)
  % A normal stress test 6 months ago has limited durability but does
  % offer modest reassurance against fixed flow-limiting CAD; warning
  % is that stress tests miss non-obstructive plaque that can rupture.
  % LR ~0.5.
  source "Greenwood JP et al. CE-MARC. Lancet 2012;379:453-460."
  trust empirical

contributes 0.6065 from prior_workup_result(normal) to diagnosis(stable_angina)
  % Negative stress 6 months prior modestly lowers probability of
  % flow-limiting stable CAD, though progression in 6 months is possible.
  source "Greenwood JP et al. CE-MARC. Lancet 2012;379:453-460."
  trust empirical

contributes 2.7183 from coronary_artery_calcium_score(elevated) to diagnosis(stable_angina)
  % Any elevated CACS materially raises probability of obstructive CAD
  % vs CACS=0 (DLR for CAC=0 ruling out is ~0.4; converse direction).
  source "Detrano R et al. Coronary calcium as a predictor of coronary events in four racial or ethnic groups (MESA). NEJM 2008;358:1336-1345."
  trust authoritative

contributes 7.3891 from coronary_artery_calcium_score_value(above_200) to diagnosis(stable_angina)
  % CACS >100 is "moderately high" and >300 puts a patient near the
  % ~10x hazard tier in MESA. CACS >200 is solidly in the
  % obstructive-CAD-likely zone for symptomatic patients. LR ~7.
  source "Greenland P et al. CAC scoring and risk classification (MESA). JAMA 2004;291:210-215; Detrano et al. NEJM 2008;358:1336."
  trust authoritative

contributes 2.7183 from coronary_artery_calcium_score_value(above_200) to diagnosis(acute_coronary_syndrome)
  % CACS quantifies plaque burden, which is the substrate for plaque
  % rupture / unstable angina. Indirect but meaningful for ACS. LR ~2.7.
  source "Hecht HS et al. Clinical indications for coronary artery calcium scoring in asymptomatic patients. JACC Cardiovasc Imaging 2017;10:1187-1208."
  trust empirical

contributes 1.6487 from medication(atorvastatin_moderate_intensity) to diagnosis(stable_angina)
  % Being on a statin is a marker of recognized ASCVD risk; mildly
  % positive signal for underlying CAD substrate.
  source "Grundy SM et al. 2018 AHA/ACC cholesterol guideline. Circulation 2019;139:e1082."
  trust empirical

% no rule: medication(clonazepam) — Treats anxiety; no direct diagnostic
% bearing on cardiac ischemia probability that isn't already captured by
% the PMH(anxiety) skip above.

% no rule: medication(citalopram) — Same as clonazepam: anxiety/depression
% therapy; QT-prolongation risk irrelevant to current queries.

% no rule: medication(pantoprazole) — Treats GERD; redundant with PMH(gerd) skip.

% no rule: medication_regimen(as_needed) — Administrative dosing detail;
% no diagnostic weight for queries.


% ---------- VITAL SIGNS ----------

contributes 0.7408 from vital_signs(within_normal_limits) to diagnosis(acute_coronary_syndrome)
  % Hemodynamic stability is reassuring against high-risk ACS subsets
  % (Killip class >I, shock) but does not rule out NSTEMI / UA. LR ~0.7.
  source "Amsterdam EA et al. 2014 AHA/ACC NSTE-ACS Guideline. Circulation 2014;130:e344-e426."
  trust authoritative

% no rule: temperature(afebrile) — Subsumed by vital_signs(within_normal_limits).
% no rule: blood_pressure(normal) — Subsumed.
% no rule: respiratory_rate(normal) — Subsumed.
% no rule: oxygen_saturation(normal) — Subsumed; would matter for PE differential.
% no rule: supplemental_oxygen(none) — Subsumed by saturation/RR.

contributes 0.8187 from heart_rate(low_normal) to diagnosis(acute_coronary_syndrome)
  % Sinus bradycardia is not a feature of acute ischemia (which usually
  % drives sympathetic tachycardia); mild evidence against. LR ~0.8.
  % Also consistent with beta-blocker effect or athletic conditioning.
  source "Amsterdam EA et al. Circulation 2014;130:e344-e426."
  trust empirical

% no rule: weight(normal_to_overweight) — BMI ~25 is near neutral on CAD risk.
% no rule: height(six_feet) — No diagnostic weight.


% ---------- PHYSICAL EXAM ----------

contributes 0.7408 from physical_examination(unremarkable) to diagnosis(acute_coronary_syndrome)
  % Absence of new murmur, gallop, JVD, rales modestly lowers
  % probability of high-risk ACS / complicated MI. LR ~0.7.
  source "Amsterdam EA et al. Circulation 2014;130:e344-e426."
  trust authoritative

% no rule: cardiac_exam(regular_rate_and_rhythm) — Subsumed by
% physical_examination(unremarkable).
% no rule: cardiac_exam(normal_s1_s2) — Subsumed.
% no rule: pulmonary_exam(clear_to_auscultation_bilaterally) — Subsumed;
% would matter to rule out CHF/pneumonia.


% ---------- LABS ----------

% no rule: comprehensive_metabolic_panel(unremarkable) — Renal function
% affects troponin interpretation but normal CMP here just confirms no
% confounder.

% no rule: hemoglobin_hematocrit(mildly_decreased) — Mild anemia can be
% an anginal trigger and modestly affects oxygen delivery, but the LR
% for any of the queries is small and bidirectional.
% no rule: hemoglobin_value(mildly_low) — Refines the term above; same logic.
% no rule: hematocrit_value(mildly_low) — Same.
% no rule: coagulation_studies(unremarkable) — Pre-procedural lab; no
% diagnostic LR for the queries.

contributes 0.0821 from cardiac_biomarkers(within_normal_limits) to diagnosis(acute_coronary_syndrome)
  % Normal cardiac biomarkers in the ED rule out NSTEMI with high NPV
  % when serial measurements are negative. This aggregate term is
  % reinforced by the more specific high-sensitivity troponin contribs
  % below; we keep its magnitude moderate to avoid double-counting.
  % LR ~0.08.
  source "Twerenbold R et al. NEJM 2019;380:2529-2540 (APACE)."
  trust authoritative

% no rule: creatine_kinase_mb(below_threshold) — CK-MB is superseded by
% hs-troponin per 2021 AHA/ACC chest-pain guideline; its independent
% diagnostic value over normal hs-cTn is negligible.

contributes 0.1353 from high_sensitivity_troponin_i_first(normal) to diagnosis(acute_coronary_syndrome)
  % First hs-cTnI below the 99th percentile contributes to the ESC 0h
  % rule-out limb. Alone it is not sufficient; paired with a second
  % normal value it achieves ~99.7% NPV. LR ~0.135.
  source "Twerenbold R et al. NEJM 2019;380:2529-2540."
  trust authoritative

contributes 0.0821 from high_sensitivity_troponin_i_second(normal) to diagnosis(acute_coronary_syndrome)
  % Second normal hs-cTnI 3h later completes serial rule-out. Combined
  % with the first measurement, the ESC 0/1h or 0/2h algorithm gives
  % NPV ~99.7-99.8% for NSTEMI. LR ~0.08.
  source "Twerenbold R et al. NEJM 2019;380:2529-2540; ESC 2023 NSTE-ACS Guideline."
  trust authoritative

contributes 1.0000 from high_sensitivity_troponin_i_second(normal) to diagnosis(stable_angina)
  % Normal troponin does NOT rule out stable angina; by definition
  % stable angina has no myocyte necrosis. Net-zero diagnostic weight.
  source "Fihn SD et al. Circulation 2012;126:e354-471."
  trust consensus


% ---------- IMAGING / ECG ----------

contributes 0.6065 from chest_xray(negative_for_pneumothorax_opacities_free_air) to diagnosis(acute_coronary_syndrome)
  % CXR primarily rules out competing differentials (pneumothorax,
  % pneumonia, perforation, aortic dissection signs); normal CXR
  % modestly raises relative probability of cardiac etiology by
  % eliminating alternatives.
  source "Gulati M et al. 2021 AHA/ACC chest-pain guideline. Circulation 2021;144:e368-e454."
  trust authoritative

contributes 0.3679 from electrocardiogram(no_acute_st_t_changes) to diagnosis(acute_coronary_syndrome)
  % Normal/unchanged ECG halves the probability of ACS (especially
  % STEMI is excluded). Does NOT rule out NSTEMI/UA: ~50% of NSTEMI
  % present with non-diagnostic ECGs. LR ~0.37.
  source "Pope JH et al. Missed diagnoses of acute cardiac ischemia in the ED. NEJM 2000;342:1163-1170."
  trust authoritative

contributes 0.8187 from electrocardiogram(sinus_bradycardia) to diagnosis(acute_coronary_syndrome)
  % Sinus bradycardia (vs sinus tach or new arrhythmia) is weakly
  % against acute ischemia in the absence of inferior MI vagal pattern.
  source "Amsterdam EA et al. Circulation 2014;130:e344-e426."
  trust empirical


% ---------- INTERACTIONS ----------

interacts 4.4817 when chest_pain(exertional_substernal_intermittent) and symptom_relief(rest)
  for diagnosis(stable_angina)
  % The Diamond-Forrester typical-angina triad is super-additive: each
  % criterion alone is weakly to moderately positive, but the combination
  % is what defines "typical angina" and drives PTP to ~87% in a 40-49
  % male. The extra interaction term captures the non-linearity.
  source "Diamond GA, Forrester JS. NEJM 1979;300:1350-8."
  trust authoritative

interacts 4.4817 when symptom_progression(worsening) and recent_worsening_window(two_weeks)
  for diagnosis(acute_coronary_syndrome)
  % A chronic worsening trajectory PLUS marked acceleration in the last
  % two weeks is the canonical Braunwald class I unstable-angina pattern,
  % a form of ACS. Synergistic above each contrib alone.
  source "Braunwald E. Circulation 1989;80:410-414; Amsterdam EA et al. Circulation 2014;130:e344-e426."
  trust authoritative

interacts 4.4817 when recent_worsening_window(two_weeks) and exertional_tolerance(severely_limited)
  for diagnosis(acute_coronary_syndrome)
  % Crescendo + new CCS-IV functional limitation is the high-risk UA
  % phenotype that drives admission and invasive workup regardless of
  % biomarkers.
  source "Amsterdam EA et al. Circulation 2014;130:e344-e426."
  trust authoritative

interacts 4.4817 when coronary_artery_calcium_score_value(above_200) and chest_pain(exertional_substernal_intermittent)
  for diagnosis(stable_angina)
  % Documented atherosclerotic substrate (CACS >200) in a patient with
  % typical-angina semiology synergistically raises probability of
  % obstructive CAD as the symptom etiology.
  source "Hecht HS et al. JACC Cardiovasc Imaging 2017;10:1187-1208."
  trust authoritative

interacts 0.1353 when high_sensitivity_troponin_i_first(normal) and high_sensitivity_troponin_i_second(normal)
  for diagnosis(acute_coronary_syndrome)
  % SERIAL negative hs-cTn — not just a single value — is what delivers
  % the ESC 0/1h algorithm's 99.7-99.8% NPV for NSTEMI. The interaction
  % captures the protocol effect beyond each measurement's marginal LR.
  % Note: still does NOT rule out unstable angina, which is captured by
  % keeping the UA-driving terms (crescendo, exertional limit) intact.
  source "Twerenbold R et al. NEJM 2019;380:2529-2540; ESC 2023 NSTE-ACS Guideline."
  trust authoritative


% ---------- DISPOSITION RULES ----------

contributes 4.4817 from chest_pain(exertional_substernal_intermittent) to disposition(admit_for_further_cardiac_workup)
  % Typical-angina semiology with intermediate-to-high pretest CAD
  % probability is a class I indication for further workup (CCTA,
  % functional stress, or invasive) per the 2021 AHA/ACC guideline.
  source "Gulati M et al. Circulation 2021;144:e368-e454."
  trust authoritative

contributes 4.4817 from symptom_progression(worsening) to disposition(admit_for_further_cardiac_workup)
  % Worsening pattern shifts patient from low- to intermediate-risk
  % HEART score / EDACS strata, triggering observation or admission.
  source "Backus BE et al. Chest pain in the ED: the HEART score. Crit Pathw Cardiol 2010;9:164-169."
  trust authoritative

contributes 7.3891 from recent_worsening_window(two_weeks) to disposition(admit_for_further_cardiac_workup)
  % Crescendo angina (Braunwald class I unstable) is a class I indication
  % for admission and early invasive evaluation per 2014 AHA/ACC NSTE-ACS
  % guideline, even with negative biomarkers.
  source "Amsterdam EA et al. Circulation 2014;130:e344-e426."
  trust authoritative

contributes 4.4817 from exertional_tolerance(severely_limited) to disposition(admit_for_further_cardiac_workup)
  % CCS class III-IV symptoms reaching threshold of inability to perform
  % minimal exertion is a guideline indication for admission and
  % expedited workup.
  source "Amsterdam EA et al. Circulation 2014;130:e344-e426."
  trust authoritative

contributes 2.7183 from coronary_artery_calcium_score_value(above_200) to disposition(admit_for_further_cardiac_workup)
